WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.760
Nine years on, Canada and China revive a currency swap, easing tariffs for exporters. This is Omni View North America, Episode 50. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. After that, a court filing over a newspaper sources, a lawsuit on California's death row, and a hold on money for an Ontario auto plant, then both sides and progress watch. Prime Minister Mark Carney sat with President Xi Jinping in Shen Zhen on Tuesday, Zhenhua reported,

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.440
before the 33rd Asia-Pacific leaders meeting on the 18th and 19th of November.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.660
The New York Times reported that the two announced a trade pact ahead of that summit.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.320
Anadolu Agency reported tariff relief between the governments.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:46.220
Yahoo Finance Canada reported wider Chinese access for pork as Carney loosened steel restrictions.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:52.060
On his first full day there, CBC reported, he announced an expansion of current tariff agreements,

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.200
more flights, and deals on education in the arts.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.080
G called a better relationship the right choice for both peoples and for peace, stability,

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.760
development and prosperity, and said China is ready to push the strategic partnership

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.400
the two launched earlier this year.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:12.320
He wants deeper work and trade, energy, agriculture and finance, and new work in the green economy,

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.420
e-commerce and the digital economy.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:18.700
Karni said the relationship has been on the right track since that partnership, and

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:24.320
that Canada will press cooperation on trade, investment, new energy, farm products, artificial

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:29.080
intelligence and tourism. Shrink the list of irritants and link in the list of joint work.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:35.460
CFJC today reported he is also set to meet Mexican President Claudia Scheinbaum while both are in China.

00:01:36.532 --> 00:01:41.112
The Trump administration sought LinkedIn data to identify sources for a New York Times article.

00:01:41.532 --> 00:01:45.992
The paper reported from a court filing. That filing says the hunt has run on two parallel

00:01:45.992 --> 00:01:52.052
fronts. Both fronts sit inside one overarching investigation. Governor Gavin Newsom is being sued

00:01:52.052 --> 00:01:56.912
by victim advocates over his push to empty California's death row. The New York Times reported.

00:01:57.412 --> 00:02:02.732
The paper said he is trying to spare 548 prisoners there. Prosecutors and victims' families

00:02:02.732 --> 00:02:07.392
say that is an abuse of power. Premier Doug Ford is holding off on fresh cash for the

00:02:07.392 --> 00:02:10.072
Stellantis plant in Brampton. Global news reported.

00:02:10.672 --> 00:02:14.712
The minister who handles the province's tear for response said Ontario is willing to

00:02:14.712 --> 00:02:19.132
offer Stellantis more money to stay in that city. A premier's pause and a minister's

00:02:19.132 --> 00:02:24.784
offer are both now on the record. Dawson College in Montreal has students and faculty rallying

00:02:24.784 --> 00:02:30.024
around Luisa Juliana Chavez-Munoz, ordered out of Canada with her family by the end of December.

00:02:30.484 --> 00:02:34.604
Global News reported. Classmates and teachers want her allowed to finish school first.

00:02:35.124 --> 00:02:39.704
She said the family got the removal notice on October 15th, seven years after they arrived.

00:02:40.184 --> 00:02:44.464
On Monday, the campus started writing to several members of Parliament, hoping pressure would let

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:44.924
them stay.

00:02:45.404 --> 00:02:50.044
The office of Alexandra Mendes, the member for Brossard St. Lambert, said it is working

00:02:50.044 --> 00:02:52.764
with the family and would not say more, citing privacy.

00:02:53.204 --> 00:02:57.264
She said they came from Colombia to seek asylum because of violence and death threats against

00:02:57.264 --> 00:02:57.724
her mother.

00:02:58.204 --> 00:02:59.124
That claim was denied.

00:02:59.624 --> 00:03:04.124
She said she left as a child, has no ties left in Colombia, and that her only childhood

00:03:04.124 --> 00:03:06.624
friend was killed as an indirect result of the violence.

00:03:07.224 --> 00:03:11.344
About going back, she said, now that she's gone, I would have to relive the whole thing.

00:03:11.344 --> 00:03:16.804
Two years ago the family asked for permanent residency on humanitarian grounds. Canada's

00:03:16.804 --> 00:03:21.044
immigration department said that file does not stop a removal order, that the file will

00:03:21.044 --> 00:03:25.324
still be reviewed, and that the review could take several years. She said the family has

00:03:25.324 --> 00:03:30.184
already paid $28,000 in tuition, and that the courses do not transfer outside Quebec.

00:03:30.784 --> 00:03:35.464
Cat said a finished CJEP program would be a recognized credential, and that leaving early

00:03:35.464 --> 00:03:39.724
would mean the work already done would not amount to a degree. Teachers and students called

00:03:39.724 --> 00:03:43.444
the handling inhumane and asked why she cannot stay long enough to finish.

00:03:43.944 --> 00:03:47.284
The order, as the family has it, puts them out by the end of December.

00:03:47.824 --> 00:03:53.824
Also today, Buncombe County, the Asheville Citizen Times reported, is planning $62.4 million

00:03:53.824 --> 00:03:56.444
